{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1786916919857116001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"dragonish-sylphic-sheep","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"3040b9d5da1dfa93ea78221d06a284286f7d680f19bcbd9d7a1b1de73c0c8a28","event_uuid":"68a1ce1e-b4aa-4623-b342-3911f1e751c0","position":{"commit_sha":"2bb85d35fb42e84c81e7137f738e3f235985bb98","position":"1786914866214820001-68a1ce1e-b4aa-4623-b342-3911f1e751c0"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"41414dd8ebaed03a06762ab144b5a66f3dbd323e9d0fdfabee86fbc5d889629f","event_uuid":"722a94a9-a1e5-4786-848b-8b0057d725e4","position":{"commit_sha":"20f4573308fea4d5253e2b3427920c42d3b326c8","position":"1786914888749623001-722a94a9-a1e5-4786-848b-8b0057d725e4"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"6a69d4576109eec0dbcc04b0a2fd4d565848ca956c04f25da9b09bed825e704b","event_uuid":"7f5b9c76-08e7-4e57-be31-2eb4719f93e0","position":{"commit_sha":"f914258799570f3d931c899f1cd4d8075f662e19","position":"1786914967354109001-7f5b9c76-08e7-4e57-be31-2eb4719f93e0"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"## AWAITING USER DECISION — pydantic-ai v2 OpenAI API semantics\n\nEvidence: current tests exercise custom OpenAI-compatible endpoints through `infer_model` and pydantic-ai warns that the existing `openai:` prefix will change meaning in v2 from Chat Completions to Responses. Choosing a replacement prefix is behavioral, not a mechanical deprecation cleanup.\n\n**A — Preserve Chat Completions (recommended):** change rebar-owned model construction to `openai-chat:`. This preserves today's wire protocol and broad custom-endpoint compatibility; held-out provider-parity tests must prove no outbound payload change.\n\n**B — Migrate to Responses:** use `openai-responses:` and intentionally adopt the newer API. This may change payloads, structured-output behavior, streaming, and endpoint compatibility; it requires explicit parity evidence and migration documentation.\n\n**C — Defer with a dependency bound:** retain `openai:` and pin pydantic-ai below v2 temporarily. This avoids an immediate behavior choice but carries upgrade debt and leaves the warning unresolved.\n\nRecommendation: approve A unless there is a product goal to adopt Responses now. No code, claim, or implementation work will begin until the user selects the intended behavior.","timestamp":1786914967354109001}],"created_at":1786914866214820001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"722a94a9-a1e5-4786-848b-8b0057d725e4","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"0024-fa99-d5bb-49bc"}],"description":"## Context\nThe default suite passes but five OpenAI-compatible provider tests emit `PydanticAIDeprecationWarning`: in pydantic-ai v2.0 the `openai:` model prefix will resolve to the Responses API by default; callers must use `openai-chat:` to preserve current Chat Completions behavior or opt into `openai-responses:` explicitly. The warning originates from `src/rebar/llm/runner.py:389` and test helper calls to `infer_model`.\n\n## Reproduction\nRun the named OpenAI-compatible provider unit tests with Pydantic AI deprecations promoted to errors. Current model inference emits the warning.\n\n## Plan\nUse rebar-debug to trace every configured OpenAI-compatible model path and prove which API semantics rebar currently promises. Present a behavior decision before changing prefixes if Chat Completions versus Responses changes payloads, structured output, or endpoint compatibility. Then repair all confirmed surfaces under held-out RED warning-as-error and provider-parity oracles.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] All model-prefix construction and inference surfaces are inventoried with caller evidence.\n- [ ] The chosen Chat Completions or Responses behavior is explicitly approved before any semantic change.\n- [ ] OpenAI-compatible provider tests pass with Pydantic AI deprecation warnings promoted to errors.\n- [ ] Structured-output and custom-endpoint parity remains green across supported providers.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["warning","pydantic-ai","provider"],"ticket_id":"1d22-40ba-8e2b-4f67","ticket_type":"bug","title":"OpenAI-compatible provider uses pydantic-ai prefix with announced v2 semantic change","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["68a1ce1e-b4aa-4623-b342-3911f1e751c0","722a94a9-a1e5-4786-848b-8b0057d725e4","7f5b9c76-08e7-4e57-be31-2eb4719f93e0"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786916919857116001,"uuid":"c96dab86-7f0d-4415-80fb-f0bf2b1968c6"}